// FROST FORTRESS — SNOW GLOBE — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FROST FORTRESS as kawaii future bass — a game alternate of frost, selectable from the
// dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// 140 in half time, glittering and sweet: the hook sung by a vowel chop (aah eeh ooh eh
// oh, a vowel a note) with a music box an octave over it, supersaw chords stuttering in
// eighths over an 808, a crystal sparkle and a "yoi" wub in the gaps. The harmony takes
// frost's D minor to its relative major — Dm9 Bbmaj9 | F C, vi–IV–I–V in F — which
// every note of the hook already belongs to. The drop grows the one-bar hook into
// eight by sequencing it up the scale, a third then a fifth.
// 
// It starts somewhere unexpected — bars 1–4 are the DROP without its drums, as if heard
// from inside the globe. There is a FALSE ENDING (the music box alone, then nothing),
// and the second drop comes back in FULL TIME with a plain square doubling the hook.
// 
//   1–4    cold open — the drop's chords and hook, no drums (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    build — the hook climbing a third at a time, snare roll, filter, riser
//   9–24   drop — half time: stutter chords, vowel chop + music box, 808, yoi wub
//   25–32  break — the hook at half speed on a bright grand, Dm9 Fmaj9 Dm9 Bbmaj9;
//          then at its own speed as the kit creeps back
//   33–36  build two
//   37–38  false ending — the music box alone; a beat of nothing; a pickup
//   39–54  drop two — FULL TIME, the square doubling the hook, everything up
//   55–58  outro — the music box winding down; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// Cabinet sync kept: frost-3's sleigh carol takes its key from the first bass note of
// the section it lands in, so every bar pair starts on D; the generator asserts it.
// 
// 58 bars at 140, 99s. Written by
// work/local/_frost-remix-snow-globe.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs;
// re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-stops.mjs): the false ending is dead air — every lane cut on bar 38 and the master silent until the pickup on beat 4.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): the whole mix opens an eighth at a time over the build (5–8).
//
